  ],
  "notes": "Not expressible: the single-NAT-by-default vs one-per-AZ mode (the prompt names no variable, and the NAT count is only in locals). 'Allocates their CIDRs from the VPC range per availability zone' is not checked: the allocation lives in locals (invisible), and the previous regex on 'cidr' was true for any subnet. 'Not created unless subnet definitions are supplied' is checked as: the default plan holds exactly one resource across the VPC/subnet/gateway/route/subnet-group types. Public/private classes are not checked by name; 'intra' is checked as a declared subnet/route-table mentioning it. Subnet-dependent resources are checked as declared since defaults create only the VPC. 'In us-east-1' is not observable (the adapter plans every resource in us-east-1). The module toggle is checked on the VPC's count/for_each gate only, not on every resource. The ClassicLink extra was removed: the attribute no longer exists in current AWS providers."
